 yeah  i'm also a concert photographer and i  photographed you in concert so i've seen  first hand that connection that you have  with your fans in that sense  what's it like to hear so many of those  stories over the years of your career  and to hear  about so many people whose lives you've  helped does it feel like both this  beautiful blessing and really kind of  the heaviest burden to hear the pain  that  all of these other people have gone  through but how you've helped to uplift  them  well it's definitely feel it's a  beautiful blessing but it's a  responsibility now  you know it's like wow you know but at  the same time  you know what i love about my fans is  that they know  that my life is imperfect as well and  i'm not going to always get it right  but they respect the fact that i respect  that this is  responsibility you know that i know that  they their children  they have children now that i have to  look out for you know  so you know they it's a beautiful thing  but  you know it's it's a huge responsibility  did you understand the rules and the  boundaries that you were breaking early  on in your career or was that something  that you also  needed some time and reflection to come  to that conclusion  i had no idea what i was doing early in  my career i was afraid  i was on guard i didn't trust anybody  and i just was going  off on anyone that would invade that  space  you know um i didn't know what i was  doing until later i found out you know  that i wasn't doing a lot of things  right and i had to you know i was  hurting a lot of people was hurting  because i was hurting myself  and i had to grow up and realize that my  life is my life  you know i have to be responsible for  my life you've seen  this that you've pretty much done  everything that you wanted to do  so once you get to that point how do you  figure out what's next  how do you continue to keep things  interesting and exciting for yourself  and to be inspired  well you i think you go for the most  challenging thing the thing that you're  probably the  you know the most afraid of something  that you can learn you know  from and you just challenge it like with  acting that thing  i was you know i've been acting you know  in little things since like 1996  but you know these big movies like  mudbound and this show like um  you know ghosts and you know it's those  are challenging things so i think you  just go through for the most challenging  thing  and the thing that you've never done  before like the production company i've  never done that before i have a  production company that i'm  seriously involved in and you know  when you're entertainment at some point  you want to be behind the camera or you  want to be  you know producing something  what stands out to you more the first  time you heard one of your songs on the  radio or the first time you saw  a movie poster or a trailer for  something you had an acting role in  the first time i heard my song on the  radio that stands out  because i knew that moment i was going  to be able to  take my family you know out of the miser  the misery in the  environment we was living in i knew that  i was gonna be able to  save us you know like get us that that's  that's how i felt about that moment like  you know how i get to get my mother out  of these projects i get to get my  sisters and you know my family  out of here when it comes to acting  roles  do you have like a dream project you'd  like to do is there somebody  from history or from some sort of source  material you'd love the opportunity to  play  you know i don't right now i'm just  trying to focus on what i'm doing i  don't have a dream  except to be great at what i'm doing  right now with this tv show  have you found that you enjoy especially  after doing you know you have this show  but you also did the umbrella academy  before that  are you enjoying getting to spend a bit  longer period of time with the character  and getting to really  delve into someone yes i love it  um i love cr the the writer  you know that writes this stuff and i  love being able to feel  or you know fill in this character with  all these real  places i have to travel i love it yeah  if someone told you 25 years ago when  you put  this album out that you'd be where you  are now how would you have reacted to  that do you think the younger version of  you  would have just thought that was crazy  yes  i would have been like yeah whatever  right  how do you think that version of you  would feel about  the the life path you've had i mean  would that you how i mean how excited  would they be about  that that me would not be able to handle  any of this because  you have to be you have to be um a  mature  a more mature responsible kind person  and  that person wasn't too kind she wasn't  responsible  she didn't trust anybody she was bad  i love that you can reflect on that now  though so that's that's the important  part  well awesome i appreciate you talking to  me about this so much i loved  how this film was done and and thank you  thank you christina

